    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d925">

                <pb facs="1019" n="1007" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg1007"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390D.11/196: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-09T18:00:00+02:00">May 9, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 9—4:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>50. Department’s 26, April 26, 4 p.m. Being apprehensive of a deadlock in our
                    negotiations I discussed the matter yesterday with the Foreign Minister.<anchor
                        n="65" xml:id="d925-f1"/> He said that he himself was not yet fully
                    convinced that our proposals were altogether satisfactory. He promised, however,
                    to interest himself personally in trying to work out a satisfactory
                    arrangement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
